            title: 'Scholarly Perspective: Cold War Consensus',
            body: "Historians point to the early support for the war as the peak of the post-WWII 'Cold War consensus.' During this era, both political parties and the general public shared the unquestioned belief that global communism posed a mortal threat to US security, making military intervention in places like Vietnam seem not only justified but necessary.",
